{title: Fire Shut Up In My Bones}
{key: C}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Jerusalem was a shaking, Pentecost had arrived,
An upper room party, And they were drunk on the new wine,
Jesus stood [C]among them, And they knew there was no [F]doubt,
This [C]Holy Ghost [F]fire will make you [C]dance and shout.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]It's just like fire, shut up in my bones.
It's the [F]Holy Ghost fire, shut up in my bones.
It's just like [C]fire, and it's shut up in my [F]bones.
It's the Holy Ghost [C]fire, and it's shut up in my bones.[F]

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]From his mother's belly, Born to prophesy.
The prophet [C]Jeremiah, Would lift his voice and cry.[F]
Be quiet folks [C]commanded, Shut up leave us [F]alone.
How can you be quiet, [C]When there's fire down in your bones.[F]

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]Into an open sepulcher, Upon Elizah's bones,
The dead man [C]resurrected, And he ran back to his home,[F]
When he tells the [C]folks the story, You could [F]hear him say,
I found that Holy [C]power, In a dead man's grave.[F]

{comment: Verse 4}
[C]Some people get offended, Because I leap and shout,
They say to [C]much emotion, And to much moving about,[F]
Don't tell me to be [C]silent, Or sit down in my [F]pew,
Cause if you felt what I [C]felt, I know you'd be shouting too.[F]
